# System unit: installed to /etc/systemd/system/ by deploy/install.sh. cage
# (a single-window Wayland compositor) on tty1 runs deploy/kiosk: the panel
# turned to portrait and Chromium full screen on brick-panel.service's page.
[Unit]
Description=brick-panel kiosk (cage + Chromium) on tty1
After=systemd-user-sessions.service plymouth-quit-wait.service brick-panel.service
Wants=brick-panel.service
Conflicts=getty@tty1.service lcars-kiosk.service brick-kiosk.service
After=getty@tty1.service

[Service]
User=zaphod
PAMName=login
TTYPath=/dev/tty1
TTYReset=yes
TTYVHangup=yes
TTYVTDisallocate=yes
StandardInput=tty-fail
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal
UtmpIdentifier=tty1
UtmpMode=user
Environment=XDG_SESSION_TYPE=wayland
# A transparent cursor theme (deploy/blank-cursors): the touchscreen counts as
# a pointer, so cage would otherwise draw an arrow on the panel.
Environment=XCURSOR_PATH=/usr/local/share/brick-panel/cursors XCURSOR_THEME=default
ExecStart=/usr/bin/cage -d -- /home/zaphod/brick-panel/deploy/kiosk
Restart=always
RestartSec=5

[Install]
WantedBy=graphical.target
